---
import '../styles/global.css';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const site = 'https://paddlme.tech/about';

const reasons = [
  {
    title: 'Verified before you book',
    body: 'Everyone confirms their ID with a live selfie and a face match. We receive a pass or fail, not your documents.',
    paths: ['M12 3l7 3v6c0 4-3 7-7 9-4-2-7-5-7-9V6l7-3z', 'M9 12l2 2 4-4'],
  },
  {
    title: 'A recorded handover',
    body: 'The renter gets a code only they can see. The host enters it to finish the safety checklist, so neither side can skip it.',
    paths: ['M8 12a3 3 0 106 0 3 3 0 00-6 0z', 'M11.5 14.5L12 21l2-2 2 2 .5-6.5'],
  },
  {
    title: 'Reviews both ways',
    body: 'Hosts see a renter before they confirm. Renters see the host. Gear and people build a history at the same time.',
    paths: ['M12 4l2.4 4.9 5.4.8-3.9 3.8.9 5.4L12 16.4 7.2 18.9l.9-5.4L4.2 9.7l5.4-.8z'],
  },
  {
    title: 'Money stays local',
    body: 'A hire pays someone in your area rather than a depot two hours away, and puts a second use on gear that already exists.',
    paths: ['M12 21s7-6.2 7-11a7 7 0 10-14 0c0 4.8 7 11 7 11z', 'M12 12.5a2.5 2.5 0 100-5 2.5 2.5 0 000 5z'],
  },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>About — Paddlme</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Why Paddlme exists: peer-to-peer water sports hire in New Zealand, with identity verification and a recorded safety handover on every booking."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href={site} />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </head>

  <body class="bg-white font-sans text-ink antialiased">
    <Nav />

    <section class="relative">
      <img
        src="/jetski-pov.webp"
        alt="Two riders on jet skis offshore"
        class="h-[200px] w-full object-cover sm:h-[240px]"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-ocean-950/45"></div>
      <div class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center">
        <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[880px] px-8">
          <h1
            class="text-[36px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-white sm:text-[48px]"
          >
            Our purpose
          </h1>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <main class="mx-auto max-w-[880px] px-8 pb-32 pt-28">
      <p class="text-[17px] leading-[1.8] text-ink">
        Paddlme lets people rent kayaks, paddleboards and jet skis from people
        who already own them. Most of this gear sits idle. A kayak gets used a
        dozen weekends a year, a jet ski two weeks of summer, and hiring one
        usually means driving to a shop that keeps shop hours and stocks
        whatever it decided to buy.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-28 grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-24 gap-y-16 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <section>
          <h2
            class="text-[30px] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.015em] text-ocean-950 sm:text-[38px]"
          >
            Our vision
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-5 text-[16px] leading-[1.75] text-muted">
            Trying a sport should not cost the price of the equipment. If you
            want to know whether paddleboarding is for you, rent a board for an
            afternoon instead of buying one.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2
            class="text-[30px] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.015em] text-ocean-950 sm:text-[38px]"
          >
            Our goal
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-5 text-[16px] leading-[1.75] text-muted">
            A booking both sides trust. Every host and renter verifies their
            identity first. Every handover runs a safety checklist. If a paddle
            comes back chipped, there is a record of the condition it left in.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-32">
        <h2
          class="text-[30px] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.015em] text-ocean-950 sm:text-[38px]"
        >
          Why Paddlme?
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-[16px] leading-[1.75] text-muted">
          Renting from a stranger only works if both people know what they are
          getting into. These are the parts that make that possible.
        </p>

        <div
          class="mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-10 gap-y-14 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4"
        >
          {
            reasons.map((reason) => (
              <div>
                <svg
                  class="h-10 w-10 text-ocean-500"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.5"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  {reason.paths.map((d) => <path d={d} />)}
                </svg>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-[18px] font-bold text-ink">{reason.title}</h3>
                <p class="mt-2.5 text-[15px] leading-[1.7] text-muted">{reason.body}</p>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <p class="mt-32 text-[16px] leading-[1.75] text-muted">
        Paddlme is in beta on Android, starting on the Hibiscus Coast. If you
        have gear in the garage, list it. If you want to get on the water, see
        what is nearby.
      </p>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>